gerprints":{"exact":"8390137aa1c3afce077f5b824cf64bd0bb02014b78c1750993433832346118a9","compact":"4962c3560d43029ba406c75e407b7baa2dbd4ff7edbfe5ba189951809fb82244","nasal":"62bf7953819bf0bacfa7b7813dad8ebec61e33b9a6c0ff34c1ba2cec55c8ffc7"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-61-7","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":61,"verse":7,"english":"And albeit tempted by viands and objects of enjoyment and desire, the famous and highly virtuous one, plunged in grief, shall not pertake of those things.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-62-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4061007","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1b4169454aaa64d5a5254d730c9d1fac5d29a2a6f6c8552b200672defadeb63d","compact":"f216ebb35b6592d581fbd8a06f3ee9e3582aff7f2b54c8bb694e326ca2e9d9fa","nasal":"7234431246bcef8a3231b7b4ed8d69f9c06e02f10df07ba219d0d96ab08dce12"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-61-8","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":61,"verse":8,"english":"And knowing that Videha's daughter (has been fasting for many a day), Vāsava shall offer Vaidehī pāyasa like to ambrosia, difficult of being procured even by the gods.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.859,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-62-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4061008","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ae94f76aa2d6f0551cf402ef94cef0d9bd9925e521d0ee05324f89a81d8f26ae","compact":"0087db149662db73a744cdbd681758db5defdc33113f5de72e80c3848a06456f","nasal":"19b698d8367ed5315b41dbaed38d7f986295b25fcf28af39201ddc47326d3e7c"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-61-9","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":61,"verse":9,"english":"Receiving that food, Maithili, knowing that it has come from Indra,* took up a little of it from the surface, and dropped it to the earth for Rāma. *From the fact of the food not touching the earth, and other signs. It is humorous to read the explanation of the commentator as to the reason of Indra's supplying Sītā with food. If Sītā remained fasting, Rāvana would forego his attachment for Vaidehi, on seeing her altered appearance; and thus his destruction could not take place. Further, if he saw Sītā retaining her former loveliness, he could conclude that Sītā, as also Rāma, were superhuman character, and that as such they could not be agents for his destruction according to the prophecy Rāvana shall be slain by a human being. This inducing him to persist in his bellicose attitude towards Rāma, would being down ruin upon his head.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-62-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4061009","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0a3cf75b7bbe07b6622925a7a96bf2c893159f681a1859763868949c506d0c94","compact":"8cfff44ca1f96806ffb26da85c9829a8f4bb42c6ccdc7a482484d89a956f2076","nasal":"5c274159f24ff5340e165135460adbe5c9a0e49ef55212bd4ebcc0fe1b514877"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-61-10","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":61,"verse":10,"english":"Whether my husband as well as his younger brother live, or they have attained godhead, let this food serve for them.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.576,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-62-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4061010","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"865dcc17c4c5d5da9e4577198aa5c28418ca7e2d96b8bd1e1f7f69f83a7351f3","compact":"540a421fdd995cb7bb7d1906a9906d66552e9804044306dedeb9138a01916b8d","nasal":"4b696e10fd991d9538eb9a4179c633e2f8eeaf9b0f3f7edc74cefd5c9ec8331a"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-61-11","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":61,"verse":11,"english":"Rāma's envoys, having been despatched thither.* shall come hither. You should relate to them all the facts connected with the queen of Rāma. *For going to Lankā.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.477,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-62-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4061011","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"359ba9fe4b126c76c0d12131cc4dfec3b15fdf2c8add5a49d0277418be00c5bd","compact":"27837294d9d6fdc12edb46fdb44d32258f706bc6a389d17fedf11bad8d0c9706","nasal":"8f9e2246e2b9abb79f4bb80f2b4b3a823ffe000cfca48bc0b58ad149a5f2e01f"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-61-12","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":61,"verse":12,"english":"Do not by any means go hence; and in this case, whither, again, wilt you repair? Do you stay here for season and place. You shall regain your wings.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-62-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4061012","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0c8e1e8765e28499afcbda806d1c940a0adbe3745be2a0ea531c41bcb7e9af72","compact":"964e3568294602e46137860019b451309fa0b2f661abd2893a2321f6ec3e1984","nasal":"2fdec1a2581eaac9a127aae32f6a7122a68cc3bfe1f739b0b2f24a673a3aa8c8"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-61-13","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":61,"verse":13,"english":"I could this very day furnish you with wings. But, by staying here in this condition, you wilt be able to compass the welfare of the worlds.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.862,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-62-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4061013","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d7cd5da84d1af06c4f5ec37046f47a2f26771a47716f9746a9953c1fcaa28564","compact":"a80aa6e61e3f661d360fda63e5e7ce99dd91889338199e23bffd336176b36d81","nasal":"a80aa6e61e3f661d360fda63e5e7ce99dd91889338199e23bffd336176b36d81"}},{"id":"VRCE-4